From 580c276260b1eba84ce5acf2de923dd486b64d61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:46:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 09/32] Update the liveness debug page: open LivenessPage,
 preview placeholder, slower fake engine

Debug builds only, as before:
- "Open LivenessPage" opens the real page with the selected workflow,
  camera, engine and fake scenario and shows the returned LivenessOutcome
  in a card under the buttons (the debug page only logs that session's
  events meanwhile).
- "Preview placeholder": a grey silhouette instead of the camera, both on
  the LivenessPage and on the debug page, which then creates no camera view
  at all; the best-frame thumbnails and the page's model chip are hidden
  too. This is the mode for documentation screenshots: no camera picture
  appears anywhere.
- "fake 3x slower": the override liveness.fake.timeScale, for which
  LivenessServiceHolder rebuilds the fake engine with that time scale.
- LivenessServiceHolder keeps the live preview views newest last, so when
  the LivenessPage (opened over the debug page) closes, the debug page's
  view is current again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
